From 697e43e4b0ba4511b84ee1e8fc48123b6fb92c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] validation(v2): reconcile native batch and block admission

Adapt native block and batch admission while resolving inputs and state
checks in one wave. Preserve transaction-owned immutable precomputation
and caller fee constraints. Keep cs_main held across active-chainstate
lookup and prefetch submission so concurrent reset cannot invalidate it.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Add libFuzzer harnesses covering V2 v7 wire codecs, Lotus V2 VM execution,
Merklix set reconciliation, and UTXO shard fast sync.

Original-Commit: aa56a04645b27e97d6d55b9292e73c5cb6065cdf
Original-Patch: v2/024
Split-Concern: validation

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Application pass retains original native VM/batch/block admission adapter, with pre-adapter shared validation archived verbatim. Keep actual pool locking required by the shared deferred-publication scope. UNRESOLVED native parity with shared atomic capacity reservation, next-block checks, signed rollback and precomputation interfaces; do not infer safety from application or redesign native admission during this pass.

Plan-v2 owner repair: Lane B native adaptation: retain the shared reconstruction/selection and unconditional sequence-lock checks while preserving native header, transaction, and state-root behavior.

Lane-E1: Fold daemon/patches/v2/055-validation-v2-resolve-batch-inputs-and-state-checks-in-one-wave.patch into its first logical owner.
Folded-Source-Commit: fe7ae5f9da74271a669bbed0d8bd1d7a7d47008d
Folded-author Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com> 1792312411 -0700

Folded source message (verbatim):
validation(v2): resolve batch inputs and state checks in one wave

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Extract 36-byte Outpoints directly in ParseNodeFast during authenticated internal
tree walks, eliminate unchanged-sibling DB reads at non-collapsing depths in EraseAt,
and wire one-wave V2 PreChecksBatch and pre-cs_main outpoint/sighash readahead.

Original-Commit: 6b77f6b3eaa39d56184e29082fb069af38b70f4a
Original-Patch: v2/029
Split-Concern: prefetch

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Context-only three-way application repair against the preserved repaired prefix; retain the patch additions/removals and review final endpoint diff before semantics claims.

Plan-v2 owner repair: Lane B native adaptation: retain the shared reconstruction/selection and unconditional sequence-lock checks while preserving native header, transaction, and state-root behavior.

(cherry picked from commit dfac97392e43e8cfeac69291cc2aa7726b2d3f0f)

N3 context adaptation: retain SetTipMetrics adjacent to PublishChainTipSnapshot and the native block-change waiter. Native admission, overlays and block validation remain unchanged.

